# CodeRabbit CLI Loop — Local Gate Before the PR Gate

Full manual: `.cursor/skills/coderabbit-review/SKILL.md`. Sequencing SSOT:
`docs/eleva-v3/execution-plan/README.md` section 4.

## Order of operations

1. `pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test && pnpm check:api-first-actions && pnpm build`
2. `pnpm review` — CodeRabbit CLI on uncommitted changes. Fix every finding. Re-run until clean
   or the cap (max 3 rounds; exit at the cap only with zero Critical/Major; leftover Minor/Trivial
   go to the PR body "Deferred findings" table).
3. Commit (Conventional Commits, see `commit-message-format.mdc`).
4. `pnpm review:branch` — CodeRabbit CLI on all commits vs `main`. Fix, commit, re-run until clean
   or the cap (max 2 rounds, same exit rule).
5. `git push -u origin <branch>` and `gh pr create --base main` with the PR body template
   (README section 8). Body must list CLI finding counts and any declined findings with reasons.
6. On the PR: for every CodeRabbit GitHub App comment, fix + push or reply
   `Not actionable because ...`. Re-run `pnpm review:branch` after each fix batch. Max 2 App
   rounds; then summarise leftovers in one comment for the human reviewer.
7. Merge only when there are zero unresolved CodeRabbit comments, every CI check is green and a
   human has approved: `gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch`.

## Hard rules

- Never silence a finding by weakening a rule, disabling a lint, loosening a schema, deleting a
  test, or adding a `.coderabbit.yaml` filter for the file being reviewed.
- Security, RLS/`withOrgContext`, `withAudit`, vendor-SDK boundary and PHI-in-logs findings are
  never declined.
- One phase = one branch `phase-NN/<slug>` = one PR. When a phase prompt defines split slices
  (`phase-NN.1/...`, `phase-NN.2/...`), each slice is its own branch and PR with the full loop;
  the second slice branches from `main` after the first has merged. Target <= 30 files / 400
  lines; split above 60 files / 800 lines and always before 100 reviewable files (the App skips
  at 100).
- `pnpm review` needs `coderabbit auth login` once per machine; if the CLI is not authenticated,
  stop and ask the user to authenticate rather than skipping the gate.
